HTTP/REST API specialist. Delegate any task that talks to an external service over HTTP — posting/reading on social networks (Bluesky, Mastodon, Reddit), API calls to platforms (GitHub, Spotify, WHOOP, OpenAI/Anthropic, OAuth providers), webhooks, generic REST endpoints. Auth, multi-step flows, and per-service protocol details are handled inside the manager.

NOT for:
- Browser-rendered pages or interactive logins → playwright_manager
- General web search / page scraping → web_manager
- Local file work → bash_manager
- The user's own Google Workspace — Gmail, Calendar, Tasks, Docs, Drive →
  personal_admin_manager. Those have dedicated tools that already act as the
  user's authorized Google account. Google is an HTTP API, so this manager
  looks like the fit and is not: it holds none of those tools and no Google
  credentials, so the work dead-ends here hunting for a token that was never
  needed.
